Subject: [PATCH 33/33] x86+amd64: the first memory BAR was assigned address ZERO
Arch-tested: x86 amd64 ppc

TODO 0.6c. QEMU's own `info pci` reported the VGA framebuffer as

    Bus 0, device 2: BAR0: 32 bit prefetchable memory at 0xffffffffffffffff

i.e. unmapped, on BOTH x86 and amd64 — the first framing of this as an
amd64 problem was wrong. The device tree carried phys.lo = 0 for that
BAR, `" screen" open-dev` faulted downstream of the zero, and 16 MiB of
framebuffer was unreachable.

CAUSE, from the firmware's own trace with CONFIG_DEBUG_PCI:

    Configuring BARs for .../QEMU,VGA: reloc 0x0 omask 0x8
                                       mem_base 0x1000000 size 0x1000000

drivers/pci.c:2125 seeds its allocator with `mem_base =
arch->pci_mem_base`, and this arch's `default_pci_host` OMITTED the
field. So it was 0, `reloc` for the first memory BAR came out 0, and the
BAR was programmed with an address that is not an address. Every LATER
BAR looked fine — mem_base had advanced past it by then — which is why
this survived: the symptom is confined to whichever memory BAR happens to
be configured first, and on QEMU's `pc` that is the framebuffer.

Every other arch in the tree already sets it: ppc 0x80000000, sparc64
0x20000000, both with the comment "avoid VGA at 0xa0000". x86 and amd64
never did. Reading source alone would not have found this — I checked the
struct against x86's first and confirmed they were byte-identical, which
is true and was the wrong question. The trace answered it.

AFTER, on both arches:

    BAR0: 32 bit prefetchable memory at 0x40000000 [0x40ffffff]
    BAR2: 32 bit memory at 0x41000000 [0x41000fff]

WHY 0x40000000 AND NOT THE CONVENTIONAL 0xC0000000. Above this lab's RAM
(512 MiB) with room to spare, below the APIC hole at 0xFEC00000 and the
pflash window at 0xFFBE0000 — and with BIT 31 CLEAR, so every PCI address
stays a positive 32-bit value.

That last part is not cosmetic while TODO 13.2(a) is undecided.
`decode-int` zero-extends, the tree encodes pointers as ints, and a base
of 0xC0000000 would put bit 31 into every BAR address and trip 13.2(a)'s
`a-signbit-boot` guard on the next boot. The guard would be working;
forcing that decision as a side effect of a BAR fix is what would be
wrong. Verified after the change: `a-signbit-boot=0` still, across 0x2b
four-byte decodes.

WHAT THIS DID NOT FIX, measured rather than assumed: `" screen" open-dev`
STILL faults with a stack underflow after the BAR has a real address, on
x86 and amd64 alike. TODO 0.6d predicted it "may simply go away" once
0.6c was fixed. It does not. The two are independent, and 0.6d stays open
as a driver question.

Run: vga property-abi mmio-writer pmem-writer flash-writer amd64
multiboot diagnostics ppc nvram amd64-pmem dict-identity client-forth —
all 13 PASS. The change moves every PCI memory address on both arches, so
the sweep is the point.

diff --git a/arch/x86/openbios.c b/arch/x86/openbios.c
--- a/arch/x86/openbios.c
+++ b/arch/x86/openbios.c
@@ -39,6 +39,33 @@
     .vendor_id = PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,
     .device_id = PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_82441,
     .io_base = 0x1000,
+    /* LOCAL DIVERGENCE (mklab). TODO 0.6c: WITHOUT THIS THE FIRST MEMORY BAR IS
+     * ASSIGNED ADDRESS ZERO. drivers/pci.c:2125 seeds its allocator with
+     * `mem_base = arch->pci_mem_base`, and this struct omitted the field — so it
+     * was 0, `reloc` for the first memory BAR came out 0, and the BAR was
+     * programmed with an address that is not an address. Every LATER BAR looked
+     * fine, because mem_base had advanced past it.
+     *
+     * Measured with CONFIG_DEBUG_PCI on x86:
+     *
+     *   Configuring BARs for .../QEMU,VGA: reloc 0x0 omask 0x8 mem_base 0x1000000 size 0x1000000
+     *
+     * The victim is whichever memory BAR is configured first; on QEMU's `pc`
+     * that is the VGA framebuffer, 16 MiB, which is why `" screen" open-dev`
+     * faulted and why the device tree carried phys.lo = 0 for it. Every other
+     * arch in the tree already sets this — ppc 0x80000000, sparc64 0x20000000,
+     * both with the comment "avoid VGA at 0xa0000". x86 and amd64 never did.
+     *
+     * WHY 0x40000000 AND NOT THE CONVENTIONAL 0xC0000000. Above this lab's RAM
+     * (512 MiB) with room to spare, below the APIC hole at 0xFEC00000, and
+     * below the pflash window at 0xFFBE0000 — but also with BIT 31 CLEAR, so
+     * every PCI address stays a positive 32-bit value. That is not cosmetic
+     * while TODO 13.2(a) is undecided: `decode-int` zero-extends, the tree
+     * encodes pointers as ints, and a base of 0xC0000000 would put bit 31 into
+     * every BAR address and trip 13.2(a)'s `a-signbit-boot` guard on the next
+     * boot. The guard would be working; forcing that decision as a side effect
+     * of a BAR fix is what would be wrong. */
+    .pci_mem_base = 0x40000000,
     .host_ranges = {
         { .type = IO_SPACE, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = 0x1000, .len = 0 },
         { .type = 0, .parentaddr = 0, .childaddr = 0, .len = 0 }
